  "notes": "The portable C++ scenario uses only the official IEEE 1516.1 API and standard library. A second federate remains joined so the final-federate resignation rule does not apply. The owner registers an object, expects NO_ACTION resignation to report the declared FederateOwnsAttributes exception, verifies the object name remains queryable after rejection, and then resigns with DELETE_OBJECTS for cleanup.",
